Anitha and I stand in the living room.
I have the new plant in my hand.
"Where should I put this?" I ask.
Anitha looks around in the room.
"We can put it near the sofa," she says.
"My bags lie near the sofa," I say.
"There is no space there."
Then I see a small table near the window.
I go near that table.
I put the plant pot on top of the table.
The plant now sits near the window.
There is nice sunlight outside.
The January month's sunlight comes into the room.
The plant pot now sits in that sunlight.
"This is a good place," Anitha says.
